Package: SurvFitSummary
Type: Package
Title: Survival Extrapolation with Standard Parametric and Spline Models
Version: 2.0.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Gosuke",
                  family = "Homma",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "my.name.is.gosuke@gmail.com",
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6854-5627"))
Description: Fits standard parametric survival models (exponential, Weibull,
    Rayleigh, log-normal, log-logistic, Gompertz, gamma, generalized gamma and
    generalized F) and Royston-Parmar spline models to time-to-event data,
    separately for each treatment arm or jointly with the arm as a covariate.
    Summarises the data with Kaplan-Meier estimates, Cox proportional hazards
    models, the Grambsch-Therneau test and smoothed empirical hazards, and
    reports parameter estimates on the natural and transformed scales,
    covariance matrices, Cholesky factors, goodness-of-fit statistics and
    extrapolated survival for health technology assessment.
